<section>
  <h2>EXIF fields that identify your device</h2>
  <p>Make, model, lens, and a serial number in some cases.</p>
  <p>
    EXIF metadata records the device make and model, the lens, exposure settings, and sometimes a body or
    lens serial number. Editing apps add a software tag and processing history on top. None of this is
    needed to view the picture. When you remove metadata here, those fields go away as one segment, and
    the report lists the removed fields by name and count so you can verify what disappeared.
  </p>
</section>
